# Integer128 addition promotes overflow to bigint

Adds 1 to the int128 maximum to verify the result promotes to bigint instead
of failing, then adds 1 again to verify chained arithmetic keeps using the
promoted representation. Both declarations keep the static int128 type while
the runtime values use arbitrary precision.

>>> source
maximum: int128 = 170141183460469231731687303715884105727
unit: int128 = 1

overflow: int128 = maximum + unit
print(overflow)

chained: int128 = overflow + unit
print(chained)

<<< stdout
170141183460469231731687303715884105728
170141183460469231731687303715884105729

<<< stderr
